&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Description&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;description&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#description&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each row is a TCP or UDP endpoint from a Sysinternals Tcpvcon snapshot, with owning process and identifier, protocol and state, and local or remote addresses and ports. Use it to correlate collection-time network exposure with processes and other telemetry. It contains no payload or connection history, and process attribution can become stale as identifiers are reused.&lt;/p&gt;
